  "label": "User projected onto the textual label as a self-referential or ironic identification",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'public talking' as a way to identify with or mock the act of public speaking. The meme invites the user to see themselves in the trivialized label, humorously equating public speaking with 'public talking', which implies the user might be engaging in or reflecting on such an activity. There is no explicit deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you', but the satirical labeling creates an implicit projection where the viewer is invited to participate in the joke by identifying with the concept being trivialized.",
